Subject: [PATCH 0/2] Get up to date deterministically before process-email
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>

The process-email loop picked each message after only a reindex, and
each pass fetched and rebased by following shell steps written as
prose in the skill. This series moves that work into a script, run by
just get-up-to-date, which does it the same way every time:

- fetch every remote;
- rebase your unmerged trunk work onto trunk@upstream;
- rebase the mail outbox onto mail@upstream, or point it at the
  list's tip if it has nothing pending;
- start a fresh change in the mail workspace and run notmuch new.

The loop runs it before each lookup, and the skill runs the same
recipe as its step 1. What needs judgement is left to the model:
conflicted commits and patches applied upstream with edits. A
conflicting rebase still succeeds, so the script leaves those in jj
for the pass to find. It fails only when a step cannot run at all,
such as a fetch that cannot reach a remote, and the loop then stops.

The series builds on "[PATCH 0/3] Add just process-email" [1], which
adds the loop it changes. That series is not yet on trunk; its three
commits appear here as prerequisite-patch-id lines.

